gfx803 (Polaris, GCN3): warpReduce's cross-row broadcast step must use the
DPP lowering, not the RDNA-only permlanex16 one.

WHY
---
TargetInfo.cpp's warpReduce broadcast step picks between two lowerings based
on `supportDppBroadcast()`: the DPP branch uses `row_bcast:15`/`row_bcast:31`
(both valid GCN3 instructions -- gfx803 has FeatureDPP), the other branch
emits `ROCDL::PermlaneX16Op`. `v_permlanex16` is GFX10+ only and does not
exist on gfx803 -- confirmed with `llvm-mc -mcpu=gfx803`, error "instruction
not supported on this GPU". Before this patch, `supportDppBroadcast()`
returned false for every family that is not explicitly CDNA-like, so GCN3
(added by the sibling gfx803-isa-family.patch, applied before this one) fell
into the permlanex16 branch and failed to compile any kernel exercising a
>16-lane warpReduce, surfacing as
`LLVM ERROR: Cannot select: %llvm.amdgcn.permlanex16` (hit via vLLM's
_topk_topp_kernel; see rocm-gfx803/patches/triton/README.md).

RE-DIFF (2026-09-07)
---------------------
Re-diffed against triton-lang/triton @ 675c59878. The original 2026-08-21
patch touched an inline `isCDNA(getISAFamily())` check directly inside
TargetInfo.cpp's warpReduce lowering. Upstream since extracted that check
into `TargetFeatures::supportDppBroadcast()`, a named predicate on the same
class the sibling isa-family patch touches, so the fix is now one `case`
line on that method instead of a conditional-expression edit at the call
site. The call site itself (`if (supportDppBroadcast()) { ...row_bcast... }
else { ...PermlaneX16Op... }`) is otherwise unchanged from what the original
patch's header described.

WHAT
----
Adds `GCN3` to the case list in `TargetFeatures::supportDppBroadcast()`,
routing it to the same `true` branch as GCN5_1 and every CDNA family.

